{
  "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground\u0004playground": "Sandbox",
  "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)\u0004isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content": "isReady() — die Benutzeroberfläche davon abhängig machen, um Flash-of-Untranslated-Content (FOUC) zu vermeiden",
  "ready": "bereit",
  "loading…": "lädt…",
  "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links\u0004On this page": "Auf dieser Seite",
  "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'\u0004Angular i18n, the signal-first way": "Angular i18n, der Signal-First-Ansatz",
  "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'reads'/'writes' are data access, not literal reading/writing\u0004ng-linguo is a complete internationalization solution for Angular built on a SignalStore. Reads are signals, writes are store methods, and translators never see a line of HTML. Flip the language switcher above and watch every example below re-render reactively.": "ng-linguo ist eine vollständige Internationalisierungslösung für Angular, die auf einem SignalStore basiert. Lesevorgänge sind Signale, Schreibvorgänge sind Store-Methoden, und Übersetzer sehen niemals eine Zeile HTML. Betätigen Sie den Sprachumschalter oben und beobachten Sie, wie jedes Beispiel unten reaktiv neu gerendert wird.",
  "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library\u0004Setup": "Einrichtung",
  "Card title. 'store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore (a noun); 'Bootstrap' = set up / initialize\u0004Bootstrap the store": "Den Store initialisieren",
  "Card body (developer-docs tone). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(). 'store' = the SignalStore; 'loads' = fetches translations; 'Dictionaries' = the JSON translation files; 'keyed by source string' = the English text is the lookup key\u0004provideTranslate() wires up the store; it never loads automatically — restoreLang() is the explicit kick-off. Dictionaries are plain JSON keyed by source string.": "provideTranslate() verbindet den Store; er lädt niemals automatisch — restoreLang() ist der explizite Start. Wörterbücher sind einfaches JSON, das den Quellstring als Schlüssel verwendet.",
  "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'\u0004The [code]t[/code] pipe": "Die [code]t[/code] Pipe",
  "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template\u0004Translate in the template": "Im Template übersetzen",
  "Card body. 'key' = the lookup key; 'falls through to the source' = shows the original English when no translation exists; 'blank' = empty\u0004The source English string is the key. With no translation it falls through to the source, so the UI is never blank.": "Der englische Quellstring ist der Schlüssel. Ohne Übersetzung fällt es auf den Quellstring zurück, sodass die Benutzeroberfläche niemals leer ist.",
  "He was driving incredibly fast!": "Er fuhr unglaublich schnell!",
  "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'\u0004The [code][[t][/code] directive": "Die [code][[t][/code] Direktive",
  "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element\u0004Translate an element": "Ein Element übersetzen",
  "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'subscription bookkeeping' = manually managing RxJS subscriptions\u0004Reads through to the store's signals — once a dictionary loads, the directive re-renders with no subscription bookkeeping.": "Greift auf die Signale des Stores zu — sobald ein Wörterbuch geladen ist, rendert die Direktive neu, ohne manuelle Abonnementverwaltung.",
  "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim\u0004Translate in TypeScript": "In TypeScript übersetzen",
  "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'component code' = TypeScript class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'params' = the ICU parameters; 'reactive' = updates automatically\u0004The pipe's counterpart for component code. Read it inside a computed() and it stays reactive to both params and the active language.": "Das Gegenstück der Pipe für den Komponenten-Code. Lesen Sie es innerhalb einer computed()-Funktion, und es bleibt reaktiv sowohl auf Parameter als auch auf die aktive Sprache.",
  "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)\u0004Plurals": "Pluralformen",
  "Card title. 'Cardinal plurals' = counting forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals\u0004Cardinal plurals across languages": "Kardinalpluralformen in verschiedenen Sprachen",
  "Card body. EN/PL = English/Polish; one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); 'category switch' = the plural form changing\u0004EN has one/other; PL has one/few/many/other; an exact 0 variant reads better than '0'. Walk count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to see the category switch.": "EN hat one/other; PL hat one/few/many/other; eine exakte 0-Variante liest sich besser als '0'. Führen Sie 'count' durch 1, 2, 5, 22 im Polnischen, um den Kategoriewechsel zu sehen.",
  "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts\u0004Ordinals": "Ordinalzahlen",
  "Card title. 'Ordinal' = ranking forms (1st/2nd/3rd); 'categories' = the CLDR plural categories\u0004Ordinal categories": "Kategorien für Ordinalzahlen",
  "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE = English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period\u0004EN uses st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL and DE collapse to a plain '{n}.'.": "EN verwendet st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL und DE reduzieren sich auf ein einfaches '{n}.'.",
  "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'\u0004Gender select": "Gender-Selektion",
  "Card title. 'Select' = the ICU select construct (choose a variant by value), not a dropdown; 'a string' = a text value\u0004Select on a string": "Selektion basierend auf einem String",
  "Card body. 'pronoun' = he/she/they; 'gendered past-tense verb' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'count × gender' = the combination of both; 'cross-product' = every combination\u0004EN swaps the pronoun; PL swaps the gendered past-tense verb. The second line combines count × gender — a cross-product that differs per language.": "EN tauscht das Pronomen aus; PL tauscht das geschlechtsbezogene Verb in der Vergangenheitsform aus. Die zweite Zeile kombiniert Zählung × Geschlecht — ein Kreuzprodukt, das sich je nach Sprache unterscheidet.",
  "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)\u0004Number formatting": "Zahlenformatierung",
  "Card title. 'grouping' = digit-group separators in numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000); 'Locale-aware' = follows the active language\u0004Locale-aware grouping": "Locale-basierte Gruppierung",
  "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl = English/German/Polish; the figures show how each locale groups digits\u0004The :number formatter follows the active locale: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.": "Der :number-Formatierer folgt dem aktiven Gebietsschema: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.",
  "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things\u0004Context (homonyms)": "Kontext (Homonyme)",
  "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation\u0004Same word, different meaning": "Gleiches Wort, unterschiedliche Bedeutung",
  "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'gettext msgctxt' is a technical term (keep); 'note for translators' = a hint; 'sense' = meaning\u0004context is part of the key (gettext msgctxt) and doubles as a note for translators. Switch to Polish to see each sense diverge.": "context ist Teil des Schlüssels (gettext msgctxt) und dient gleichzeitig als Hinweis für Übersetzer. Wechseln Sie zu Polnisch, um zu sehen, wie sich jede Bedeutung unterscheidet.",
  "audio player\u0004Play": "Abspielen",
  "game\u0004Play": "Spielen",
  "direction\u0004Right": "Rechts",
  "correct\u0004Right": "Richtig",
  "sequence\u0004Order": "Reihenfolge",
  "purchase\u0004Order": "Bestellen",
  "no cost\u0004Free": "Kostenlos",
  "available\u0004Free": "Frei",
  "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations\u0004Rich text (slot tags)": "Rich Text (Slot-Tags)",
  "Card title. 'emphasis' = bold/italic styling; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file. The point: no HTML appears in translation files\u0004Links and emphasis without HTML in the dictionary": "Links und Hervorhebungen ohne HTML im Wörterbuch",
  "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'literal bracket' = a real [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep); 'zero by construction' = impossible by design. [[name] shows an escaped literal bracket — keep the doubled brackets\u0004Translators see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — each binds to your own ng-template tFor, with no predefined HTML. Need a literal bracket in your prose? Double the opening one. Translator content is never inserted as HTML; XSS surface is zero by construction.": "Übersetzer sehen benannte Slots wie [[name]…[[/name]] — jeder bindet an Ihr eigenes ng-template tFor, ohne vordefiniertes HTML. Benötigen Sie eine literale Klammer in Ihrem Text? Verdoppeln Sie die öffnende Klammer. Übersetzerinhalte werden niemals als HTML eingefügt; die XSS-Angriffsfläche ist konstruktionsbedingt null.",
  "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it\u0004Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started": "Lesen Sie die [docs]Dokumentation[/docs], um loszulegen",
  "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]": "Indem Sie fortfahren, stimmen Sie unseren [terms]Nutzungsbedingungen[/terms] zu",
  "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'\u0004[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone": "[warn]Warnung:[/warn] diese Aktion kann nicht rückgängig gemacht werden",
  "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly\u0004Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot": "Maskiertes [[b]bold[[/b] bleibt literal — [b]dies[/b] ist ein Slot",
  "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]": "Stimmen Sie unseren [link]Allgemeinen [b]Geschäftsbedingungen[/b][/link] zu",
  "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)\u0004ESLint & a11y": "ESLint & Barrierefreiheit",
  "Card title (colloquial). 'linter' = ESLint; 'keep the linter happy' = satisfy the lint rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text content\u0004Keep the linter happy with empty [t] elements": "Den Linter mit leeren [t]-Elementen zufriedenstellen",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'a11y' = accessibility; 'markup' = HTML; 'fallback' = the default shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page\u0004The a11y rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content flags empty headings, anchors, and buttons. A [t] element fills its text at runtime, so the source string can move out of the markup entirely — the headings on this page are empty [t] elements; only the hero keeps its text as a fallback.": "Die Barrierefreiheitsregel @angular-eslint/template/elements-content kennzeichnet leere Überschriften, Anker und Schaltflächen. Ein [t]-Element füllt seinen Text zur Laufzeit, sodass der Quellstring vollständig aus dem Markup entfernt werden kann — die Überschriften auf dieser Seite sind leere [t]-Elemente; nur der Hero-Bereich behält seinen Text als Fallback.",
  "Section heading: translating the app automatically using an AI / LLM\u0004Translating with AI": "Übersetzen mit KI",
  "Card title. 'source string' = the original English text; 'catalog' = the translation file (.po)\u0004From source string to translated catalog": "Vom Quellstring zum übersetzten Katalog",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator. 'catalogs' = translation files; 'chat model' = an LLM; 'merges the reply' = applies the response; 'clipboard copy/paste' = manual copying\u0004The extract CLI keeps gettext .po catalogs and compiles them to runtime JSON. Translate by copying a prompt into any chat model, or fully automatically: point translator at a module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, you keep the SDK and the API key. Omit translator and translation stays a clipboard copy/paste.": "Die extract CLI verwaltet gettext .po-Kataloge und kompiliert sie zu Laufzeit-JSON. Übersetzen Sie, indem Sie einen Prompt in ein beliebiges Chat-Modell kopieren, oder vollautomatisch: Richten Sie den Übersetzer auf ein Modul aus, das Ihren eigenen KI-Anbieter aufruft — ng-linguo schreibt den Prompt und führt die Antwort zusammen, Sie behalten das SDK und den API-Schlüssel. Lassen Sie den Übersetzer weg, und die Übersetzung bleibt ein manuelles Kopieren/Einfügen.",
  "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo\u0004Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.": "Erstellt mit ng-linguo · diese Sandbox ist auch eine lebendige Dokumentation.",
